##  Play a single player mode from the link 
- https://dominique-sakrisson.github.io/ace-altitude/

# This is as always a work in progress.

## Project can be run locally over your network for multiplayer experience with other clients on your network.
## This guide assumes you're on a windows machine version 10 or higher
## Before attempting to play have required tooling installed on your system:
1. git 
1. nodejs
1. npm
1. vite deploy tool



# The game can be cloned and setup to run from your local machine multiple ways for varying purposes. 
1. Single client, 1 locally running instance.
1. Multiple local clients connected via web socket, 1 locally running instance. (Mainly for testing purposes)
1. Multiple local network clients connected via web socket and local area connection.
1. Multiple public clients, 1 locally running instance broadcast with public IP address over the internet. (slow for others, based on distance )


# First clone and setup the project locally
1. clone github repo

1. In powershell etc. from the project root run command :

```
C:/u/project-location: 

npm install
```


## For quick and dirty local single-player development start the server with command

```
C:/u/project-location: 

npx vite
```


# The game can run multiple clients on the same machine with this process below. (for testing purposes)

## In powershell:  Sets value in .env for the websocket server connection
```
C:/u/project-location: 

Add-Content -Path ".\.env" -Value "VITE_WS_URL = http://localhost:3000/"
```

## Creates application bundle for the soon-to-be-run nodejs  server

```
C:/u/project-location: 

npx vite build
```

## Serve with local nodejs server
```
C:/u/project-location/server: 

npx vite build
```


# Setup for multiple clients on local network
 - (Assumes the project has been setup with the .env file for the websocket connection address)
1. Open your windows powershell, etc

1. run vite development with the host flag 
    ```
    C:/u/project-location/server: 
    npx vite --host 
    ```
    - console should display addresses to connect from

1. In your web browser of choice enter that address.
1. Each other player may now connect via that same address.



